{"title":"Career Roadmap: Space Technology / Avionics → Embedded Engineer","role":"Embedded Engineer","summary":"An Embedded Engineer develops software and hardware systems that operate inside electronic products and mission-critical systems. In the space and avionics domain, embedded systems can control sensors, communication modules, flight computers, navigation systems, power systems, actuators and onboard instrumentation.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Space Technology / Avionics"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Domain","text":"Embedded Systems, Avionics & Aerospace Electronics"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Embedded Engineer develops software and hardware systems that operate inside electronic products and mission-critical systems. In the space and avionics domain, embedded systems can control sensors, communication modules, flight computers, navigation systems, power systems, actuators and onboard instrumentation."},{"type":"p","text":"A Space Technology / Avionics graduate has a particularly relevant foundation because the specialization combines electronics, control, communication and aerospace systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical Responsibilities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Develop firmware for microcontrollers and processors"},{"text":"Interface sensors, actuators and communication modules"},{"text":"Write C/C++ embedded software"},{"text":"Work with RTOS-based systems"},{"text":"Develop device drivers"},{"text":"Debug hardware-software integration issues"},{"text":"Implement communication protocols"},{"text":"Perform hardware bring-up and testing"},{"text":"Work with real-time systems"},{"text":"Develop avionics/embedded control modules"},{"text":"Perform unit, integration and system testing"},{"text":"Analyze timing, memory and power constraints"},{"text":"Support verification and validation"}]},{"type":"